1
00:00:00,810 --> 00:00:07,569
In 2023, insurers on HealthCare.gov denied nearly one in five in-network claims.

2
00:00:07,569 --> 00:00:11,631
Fewer than one in a hundred of those denials were appealed.

3
00:00:11,631 --> 00:00:15,307
Clause is for the person holding that denial letter.

4
00:00:15,307 --> 00:00:20,187
It reads their own plan and their letter, and it only says what it can point to.

5
00:00:20,187 --> 00:00:26,230
Here's a synthetic denial for an MRI, checked against a real Ambetter plan from Texas.

6
00:00:26,230 --> 00:00:31,781
Gemini reads the key facts from the letter, and each one links to the line it came from.

7
00:00:31,781 --> 00:00:38,695
The appeal deadline is computed by code, not by the model, and it cites the federal regulation it comes from.

8
00:00:38,695 --> 00:00:44,455
Clause also checks the letter against everything a federal denial notice must include.

9
00:00:44,455 --> 00:00:50,394
This one never names the plan provision it relies on. That gap is an appeal point in itself.

10
00:00:50,394 --> 00:00:54,737
Then Gemini drafts the appeal. But it never writes free prose.

11
00:00:54,737 --> 00:01:00,438
Every sentence must quote the passage it rests on, and code checks that quote, word for word.

12
00:01:00,438 --> 00:01:05,211
Click any sentence, and the plan page opens with the passage highlighted.

13
00:01:05,211 --> 00:01:08,772
What if a sentence says something the documents don't?

14
00:01:08,772 --> 00:01:12,654
Change the claim amount to one the letter never mentions.

15
00:01:12,654 --> 00:01:17,647
The verifier rejects it. It's greyed out with the reason, and left out of the letter.

16
00:01:17,647 --> 00:01:21,897
The same pipeline checks an Explanation of Benefits (EOB).

17
00:01:22,215 --> 00:01:30,767
This out-of-network emergency visit was charged out-of-network cost-sharing. Under the No Surprises Act, it shouldn't be, so Clause flags it.

18
00:01:30,767 --> 00:01:36,636
Under the hood, every paragraph of the plan, the letter and the federal regulations gets an address.

19
00:01:36,636 --> 00:01:41,423
Gemini Flash extracts and drafts, with a fallback chain behind it.

20
00:01:41,423 --> 00:01:50,586
A grounding verifier checks every citation, and four rule tables handle deadlines, notice gaps, reason codes and surprise billing, in plain code.

21
00:01:50,586 --> 00:01:55,519
220 tests run with no network and no API key.

22
00:01:55,519 --> 00:02:02,746
The plans and regulations are real. The denial letters and EOBs are synthetic, and labelled that way.

23
00:02:02,746 --> 00:02:08,040
Clause never contacts your insurer. It drafts. You decide what to send.
